<title>USA: Alternative Living, partner buy 2 properties.</title>
<headline>Alternative Living, partner buy 2 properties.</headline>
<dateline>BROOKFIELD, Wis. 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alternative Living Services Inc said it and a development partner have jointly bought two properties in the Syracuse market for $7.6 million.</p>
<p>The $7.6 million acquisition is expected to generate about $3 million in revenues annually, the company said. The purchase is expected to close around June 30.</p>
<p>The two residences have a capacity of 159 residents.</p>
<p>Alternative Living Services owns and operates residences for elderly and people with Alzheimer's disease.</p>
<p>((--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
